 ## Workflow[m
[31m-[m
 ```[m
 Reschedule request ─► PENDING ─► slot search ─► SLOT_PROPOSED ─► candidate picks ─► re-check ─► RESCHEDULED[m
[31m-No-show            ─► PENDING ─► outreach    ─► AWAITING_RESPONSE ─► "yes" ─► SLOT_PROPOSED ─► ... ─► RECOVERED[m
[31m-                                                                   └► "no"  ─► CLOSED (recruiter informed)[m
[32m+[m[32mNo-show            ─► PENDING ─► outreach    ─► AWAITING_RESPONSE ─► "yes" ─► SLOT_PROPOSED ─► ... ─► RECOVERED[m
[32m+[m[32m                                                                   └► "no"  ─► CLOSED (recruiter informed)[m
 No slots / no reply / delivery failure ─► RETRY_SCHEDULED ─► ... ─► ESCALATED (recruiter notified once)[m
 ```[m
[31m-[m
 1. **Reschedule request** (candidate page or recruiter-logged) creates a case and runs the slot search *in the same request*, so options go out within seconds. No recruiter action.[m
 2. **Slot search** uses the recruiter's booked interviews (and the candidate's other interviews), interview duration, working hours/days, minimum notice and any availability windows the candidate entered. It offers up to `SLOT_COUNT` slots spread across different days and never re-offers the current time or slots found to be taken.[m
 3. **Confirmation** re-checks availability under a per-recruiter booking lock before updating the *existing* interview record (no duplicate interview). If the slot was taken meanwhile it is not booked; fresh options are shown instead.[m
 4. **After booking**: candidate gets a confirmation email; the recruiter gets an in-app notification (informational, no action needed) and is asked to tell the interviewer, because interviewers are free-text names without contact details.[m
 5. **No-show**: after `INTERVIEW_NO_SHOW_GRACE_MINUTES`, the interview is marked `No Show` and the candidate is emailed asking whether they want a new time (Yes → slot proposal flow, No → case closed, recruiter informed).[m
 6. **Stops automatically** when the interview is cancelled, completed (Selected/Rejected), rescheduled by the recruiter, marked attended, or deleted.[m
[31m-[m
 ### No-show detection[m
[31m-[m
 HR Assist has no attendance feed from a meeting provider, so a no-show is only ever acted on from an **explicit attendance outcome**. It is never inferred just because the scheduled time passed.[m
[31m-[m
 - After an interview's **scheduled end** + `INTERVIEW_NO_SHOW_GRACE_MINUTES`, the interviewer or recruiter clicks **Attended** or **No-show** on the interview (Hiring Pipeline → Interviews). The outcome is saved on the interview (`attendance_status`, `attendance_recorded_at`, `attendance_recorded_by`).[m
 - **No-show** opens the recovery case and sends the follow-up immediately. The scheduled sweep (below) also picks up any interview recorded as a no-show that has no case yet: outcomes recorded late (within `INTERVIEW_NO_SHOW_LOOKBACK_HOURS`, default 7 days), or a request that failed midway.[m
 - Never processed: interviews that are cancelled, completed (Selected/Rejected), rescheduled to a new time, marked attended, or still in progress or inside the grace period.[m
 - `INTERVIEW_NO_SHOW_DETECTION=auto` (opt-in) additionally treats ended interviews with **no** recorded attendance as no-shows. Use it only if interviewers reliably click **Attended**.[m
 - Idempotent: each interview occurrence (interview + original start time) gets at most one no-show case, enforced by a unique index on open cases. Concurrent sweeps cannot create a second case or send a second initial email.[m
